   "d": "2023-07-11",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "With business improving, full year 2023 revenue and adjusted profit before tax is expected to be in line with current consensus forecasts with improving product mix expected to result in earnings being more second half weighted, as set out at the time of our preliminary results.",
   "file": "20230711_AMS_Half-Year-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-09-04",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "The combined effect of these factors is expected to impact the Group's FY23 financial performance with revenues now anticipated to be approximately £124 - £127 million and adjusted pre-tax profit of approximately £25 - £27 million.",
   "file": "20230904_AMS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-09-20",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "With the exception of the royalty adjustment (impacting Q4 2023 to Q3 2026), there were no changes to the expectations for future years.",
   "file": "20230920_AMS_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-01-10",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group is pleased to report Full Year 2023 results are expected to finish towards the middle of its published guidance ranges of £124-127 million for revenue and £25-27 million for adjusted profit before tax.",
   "file": "20240110_AMS_Full-Year-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-03-13",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "These promising US marketing initiatives, good progress in AMS's established non-US markets and ongoing geographical expansion means AMS is primed to generate double-digit revenue growth in 2024, in line with expectations, and is well placed for strong growth in the short, medium and long-term.",
   "file": "20240313_AMS_Unaudited-Preliminary-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-03-13",
   "doc": "OPS",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The preliminary results were in line with guidance and detailed the significant commercial, regulatory and clinical progress being made by the Group as it continues to build its platform for growth and invest in its portfolio of next-generation products.",
   "file": "20240313_AMS_Proposed-acquisition-of-Peters-Surgical.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-07-15",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "With momentum building across all the key surgical product areas, despite continued Woundcare headwinds, the Board remains confident that the Group (excluding Peters Surgical) will generate underlying double-digit top line growth in the full year 2024, with consolidated revenues and adjusted profit before tax expected to be in line with management forecasts.",
   "file": "20240715_AMS_Half-Year-Trading-update.md",
   "gnote": "discounted: Peters Surgical acquisition"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-09-18",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Outlook remains unchanged and the Board anticipates that revenue and adjusted profit will be in line with its expectations.",
   "file": "20240918_AMS_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-01-14",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Enlarged Group performing well and in line with consensus expectations",
   "file": "20250114_AMS_Full-Year-2024-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-03-19",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The business has continued to perform well in Q1 2025, and the Board's expectations are in line with current consensus forecasts for the full year.",
